# Normalize line endings to LF in the repository regardless of a
# contributor's local core.autocrlf setting. Found this was needed while
# building apps/web on Windows: git's default Windows autocrlf=true kept
# converting checked-out files to CRLF, which then failed prettier's
# default endOfLine: "lf" on the very next `git checkout`/cherry-pick —
# a recurring, confusing false-positive CI failure for any Windows
# contributor, not a real formatting issue. `text=auto` still lets git
# detect and leave binary files (favicon.ico, images) alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
